#59013
"Entrance to the Village"
"At first glance, these fields look like a small peasant farmstead.  There

are rows of tilled earth, a well in the distance, and the bubbling sound

of what may be a brook.  You can also make out several adobe houses in

the distance, to the south.  A fenced-off area is beyond a field in the

east, but the plantlife within is fairly visible from here.  A shiny

metal gate stands to the north, blocking the only opening in the long

east-west running adobe wall.  Patches of the ground are scarred and

burnt, and piles of dead branches rest in the corner, near the wall.

"
""
